[b]Fixes[/b]
[list]
[*]Ordinary-world mode: logging in on the old Tower pad keeps you in the normal world with your items [b](in-game)[/b]
[*]Free accounts can't pickpocket; interrupted first logins no longer lock an account; public chat and logout handled [b](tests)[/b]
[*]Death handling tightened: no eating, cooking or other actions while a death resolves; zero-health saves recover [b](tests)[/b]
[*]Dropped connections log out shortly after, as in OSRS [b](tests)[/b]
[/list]

[SPOILER=Ordinary-world mode]

[i]Live native gameplay — Ordinary-world mode: logging in on the old Tower recovery pad in Lumbridge leaves the player there, with every item still in the pack (captured during review, one revision before the final merged change).[/i]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/autismoyah-hub/project-gielinor-showcase/d52a4c27bb4897d1bb53fa97314097a45b151f9d/images/server-update-2026-10/23-recovery-pad-ordinary-world.png[/img]

[/SPOILER]
[b]The Tower (server side)[/b]
[list]
[*]The Cinderworks floor now runs on the main server, sharing the normal skilling and prayer code
[*]One full run to the reward completed in a headless test: preparation, Ash Imp, Ash Warden, reward chest (500 coins and a beer), clear kept after a restart; a second independent clear is still to come [b](in-game, headless)[/b]
[*]Floor One banker: Talk-to and examine [b](in-game)[/b]
[*]Groundwork for Tower attempts (hardcore, softcore and easy life modes, save and restore) [b](tests)[/b]
[/list]

[b]Behind the scenes[/b]
[list]
[*]Every feature is checked in game by a headless test client against the real server, from a fresh test account
[*]Both development machines are building one shared test setup
[*]The public server repository now has the current source and release notes
[/list]

[b]Coming next[/b] (in progress)
